n}⁡(nx)\n$$\n\nLet $f(x)$ be the $2\\pi $-periodic extension of a function from $x\\in [-\\pi ,\\pi )$ to $x\\in R$ with the Fourier series shown above. What is the $4$th cosine Fourier coefficient of $f(x)-3?$" :question/worked-solution "The Fourier series of $f(x)$ is\n\n$$\nf(x)∼\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)+{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx).\n$$\n\nRecall that if $C$ is a constant, the corresponding Fourier coefficients of $f(x)+C$ are\n\n- ${a}_{0}+2C$ for the constant coefficient,\n\n- ${a}_{n},$ $n\\ge 1,$ for the cosine coefficients, and\n\n- ${b}_{n},$ $n\\ge 1,$ for the sine coefficients.\n\nIn our case, $C=-3.$ Therefore, $4$th cosine coefficient of $f(x)-3$ is ${a}_{4}$ (remains unchanged)."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186229720 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186229174 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f30ca427-3074-56c3-828a-1327d7b172b0" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Effects of Vertical Shifting and Horizontal Reflection on Coefficients"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "06ac0042-e258-55d3-b06c-2dcaddce1106" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{a}_{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186547331} {:answer/id #uuid "42fda2fe-8869-54c1-9994-a4a16cdfb92d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{b}_{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186547465} {:answer/id #uuid "78004f4b-bec6-56c5-b3cf-fd82e750fdf4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{b}_{6}-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186547576} {:answer/id #uuid "855ee43d-1d00-510a-9f3e-d0e267711926" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-{a}_{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186547602} {:answer/id #uuid "8d16cef1-f56a-5c7f-81ad-ad3dd97f643a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-{b}_{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 