ent :answer.type/text} :answer/value "odd" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397145}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "18bbb808-067a-5c73-a58a-7bbbccd30b52" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "odd" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397145} :answer-field/id #uuid "00839b4e-f62d-5523-b0a0-cd44b3f38d1f" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397143} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4046271d-3273-5e3f-a757-9112f2fda282" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "sine terms" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397147} {:answer/id #uuid "3f94849a-be66-556b-b362-390c2fd77a3b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "cosine terms" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397148}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3f94849a-be66-556b-b362-390c2fd77a3b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "cosine terms" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397148} :answer-field/id #uuid "d2ef1e3c-f0e2-50af-90e8-066404b32b3d" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397146}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d7903a61-d4e3-5a7b-991a-79f6efafb8b5" :question/math-academy-id "q-338682" :question/problem "Consider the function $f(x)=x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)$ on $x\\in [-\\pi ,\\pi ].$ Select the correct options below.\n\n$\\,$\nThe function $f(x)$ is\n{{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$\nConsequently, the \n{{field-2}}\nin the corresponding Fourier series of $f(x)$ must be zero." :question/worked-solution "To determine whether $f$ is even or odd, we compare $f(-x)$ and $f(x):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(-x) & =(-x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(-x) \\\\  & =-x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x) \\\\  & =-f(x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $f(-x)=-f(x),$ we have that $f$ is odd.\n\nFor Fourier series on $[-\\pi ,\\pi ],$ the cosine coefficients are given by\n\n$$\n{a}_{n}=\\frac{1}{\\pi }{\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }f(x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)\\,\\text{d}x,\n$$\n\nand the constant coefficient is\n\n$$\n{a}_{0}=\\frac{1}{\\pi }{\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nHere, $f(x)$ is odd and $\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)$ is even, so $f(x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)$ is odd. Also, $f(x)$ itself is odd.\n\nNow, the integral of an odd function over $[-\\pi ,\\pi ]$ is $0.$ Thus, ${a}_{n}=0$ for all $n\\ge 1,$ and ${a}_{0}=0.$\n\nTherefore, the function $f(x)$ is $\\text{odd}$ and the $\\text{cosine terms}$ in its Fourier series must be zero."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186547992 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186229173 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "eb295d6c-62fe-59bc-a139-49785ac98f1f" :knowledge-point/title "Using Linearity of Fourier Series"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "30534d8b-c585-5664-86ff-6a8280445feb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5{b}_{1}-2{d}_{1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186547415} {:answer/id #uuid "b6dea7e4-04e0-5bca-8657-2e8013df7dfa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2{a}_{0}-5{c}_{0}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186547711} {:answer/id #uuid "b9e73330-e560-5146-85cc-a129311d885d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5{a}_{0}-2{c}_{0}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186547714} {:answer/id #uuid "bf3ee227-aaac-5277-9bb8-c9a0551952a9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2{b}_{1}-5{d}_{1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186547726} {:answer/id #uuid "d09345f0-8979-50d6-8e4c-ad18cbc88e66" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5{a}_{1}-2{c}_{1}" :db/id #edb/ref 1759218