{0}=\\frac{1}{\\pi }{\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nHere, $f(x)$ is odd and $\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)$ is even, so $f(x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)$ is odd. Also, $f(x)$ itself is odd.\n\nNow, the integral of an odd function over $[-\\pi ,\\pi ]$ is $0.$ Thus, ${a}_{n}=0$ for all $n\\ge 1,$ and ${a}_{0}=0.$\n\nTherefore, the function $f(x)$ is $\\text{odd}$ and the $\\text{cosine terms}$ in its Fourier series must be zero."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186397481 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186229175 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "532a73e6-e026-57c9-9bad-57cd2f75b6df" :knowledge-point/title "Parity Recognition and Series Type"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d6fb8e02-c2ed-54c2-a769-c0f5e618e887" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "even" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397483} {:answer/id #uuid "82f2576e-7f7d-514c-b7d3-b07f1e9d3631" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "odd" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397484}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "82f2576e-7f7d-514c-b7d3-b07f1e9d3631" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "odd" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397484} :answer-field/id #uuid "35a58589-56cd-5637-b523-03f859fac5b6" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397482} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "34d21a9d-340e-5cb4-a005-7da885a8f606" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "sine terms" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397486} {:answer/id #uuid "1b091b7e-9971-5f89-be72-b0882bfa2d62" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "cosine terms" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397487}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1b091b7e-9971-5f89-be72-b0882bfa2d62" :answer/type {: